# Saudi Prep — cache rules for the host (Hostinger / LiteSpeed)
#
# Pages, the service worker, the manifest and the question data carry no version
# in their URL, so the browser must ask the server before reusing its copy (the
# answer is a cheap 304 when nothing changed). Without this header a browser
# guesses a lifetime from the file's age and keeps showing the previous deploy
# for hours. css/js are named with ?v=N in the pages and stay cached.
<IfModule mod_headers.c>
  <FilesMatch "\.(html|json)$">
    Header set Cache-Control "no-cache"
  </FilesMatch>
  <Files "sw.js">
    Header set Cache-Control "no-cache"
  </Files>
</IfModule>
